  "id": "PALOMAR-2026-10-21-000008-v1",
  "title": "Improved zero-density estimates for the Riemann zeta function",
  "abstract": "We establish improved zero-density estimates for the Riemann zeta function relative to the bounds previously released in PALOMAR-2026-10-11-000010 v1 and PALOMAR-2026-10-09-000005 v1. Let N(σ,T) count the nontrivial zeros with Re ρ ≥ σ and |Im ρ| ≤ T, with analytic multiplicity. For T ≥ 2 and ε > 0, our bounds have the form N(σ,T) ≤ C(σ,ε)T^((1−σ)A(σ)+ε). The native quantitative bounds improve those earlier power curves for 12/17 < σ ≤ 3/4 and 7/9 < σ ≤ 7/8. The displayed power-curve comparison continues for 7/8 < σ < 17/19, where the imported OpenAI result already gives N(σ,T)=0. Later Lean-formalized refinements also give a zero-free region below 7/8 [Collet26]; our comparisons near 7/8 concern the named earlier results. Table 1 gives all the proved contribution curves and their full ranges, including A(σ)=12/(9σ−1) on [5/7,113/153] and A(σ)=255/(153σ+7) on [113/153,3/4]. Figure 1 compares the cumulative curves.",
